 "_doc": "The source of the shared Front Range backdrop: seven USGS 3DEP 1/3 arc-second staged tiles (about 10 m cells, bare earth, heights NAVD88, horizontal NAD83; each tile is named by its NW corner and overlaps its neighbours by 6 cells). NOT in git. Fetch every url into one directory and check it against sha256; tools/backdrop_bake.py takes that directory as --dem. width / height / cell_deg / crs / nodata are as the horizon study read them (tracks/denver-grand-prix/source/horizon/horizon.3dep13.json, \"dem\"); the byte counts agree with that study's, so these are the files it measured.",
